WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:05.310
The clank of heavy metal bars echoing through
the building usually kept Javi up at night.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.340
But he never thought that he would ever come
to miss that sound one day.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:14.599
As he tossed and turned in his uncomfortable
bunk, he couldn’t help that the noise reminded

00:00:14.599 --> 00:00:19.680
of how confined he was… and how trapped
he felt within.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:25.160
It had been a mistake, an honest and completely
unpredictable mistake.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:30.050
On the nights that sleep evaded him, he’d
always replay the events over and over again.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:35.130
His daughter, Kali, calling him out of the
blue, her distorted, uncontrollable sobs playing

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.340
into his ear over the phone.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:42.190
Javi remembered jumping into his car and flooring
the accelerator, rain drumming against the

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.390
windshield
as he drove all the way across town to her

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.890
apartment in the early hours of the morning.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:52.931
And then there was the scene that awaited
him as he stepped through the door,

00:00:52.931 --> 00:00:58.180
the mess that had been of her kitchen, covering
the floor, smeared up the walls, even dripping

00:00:58.180 --> 00:00:59.990
off the ceiling.

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:04.930
It all stayed there as Javi debated with his
daughter about what they should do next.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:09.550
She was crying, begging for her dad’s help,
suggesting they should clean the place from

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:13.180
top to bottom
and hide any evidence scattered around the

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:14.180
apartment.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:18.600
Laying in his cell all those months later,
he sometimes wondered why he said no to that

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.600
idea.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.150
Instead, they came up with a story, a falsified
version of events.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:30.140
Javi made Kali swear to stick to it, no matter
what, and through heavy sobs she agreed.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:35.150
Then, after they’d been over every detail
and had it perfect, Javi got back in his car

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:39.830
and drove to the nearest police precinct to
turn himself in.

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:43.940
All while taking the fall, pleading guilty
in court and being sentenced to prison,

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:47.930
he reminded himself over and over that he
was doing it for Kali.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:53.770
No matter what she had done, whatever accidents
had happened, she was still his kid, and he’d

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:55.650
do anything to protect her.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.720
But that was part of what made it sting so
bad.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:02.170
Not being locked up, but not getting to see
her.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:06.380
Despite making request after request, Javi
was denied visitation rights,

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:10.091
when seeing his daughter and knowing she was
alright were the only things that would’ve

00:02:10.091 --> 00:02:11.770
made this struggle easier.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:16.100
It was after his twentieth request that a
guard informed Javi he was being moved.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:20.560
At first, he assumed ‘moved’ meant to
another part of the prison, maybe with more

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.990
lax security and the right to see Kali.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.740
But they didn’t mean moved.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.720
They meant transferred…

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:33.340
into the care of an organization Javi came
to know as the SCP Foundation.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.670
It was different here.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:39.030
The kind of people he was locked up with as
a member of ‘D Class personnel’ were some

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.700
of the most heinous criminals on the planet.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.950
But there was something else going on, something
weirder.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.660
Javi would overhear whispers and rumors from
the other D Classes;

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:53.970
they’d talk of experiments conducted by
the Foundation…

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.819
with them as the lab rats.

00:02:56.819 --> 00:03:01.170
“D-14164,” the researcher greeted him
as he was pulled into a side room, flanked

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:03.560
on all sides by armed Foundation guards.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.410
“Yours is quite the interesting case.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:10.930
No priors, no criminal affiliations of any
kind, hardly any family to testify to your

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:11.930
innocence.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:13.319
And yet, what you did…

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:15.569
now, that takes some guts.

00:03:15.569 --> 00:03:17.380
If you’ll pardon the pun.”

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.510
“So, it’s all true then,” Javi replied
solemnly.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.099
“You’re here to say you want to experiment
on me.”

00:03:23.099 --> 00:03:28.489
“I wouldn’t call it an ‘experiment’
per se,” the researcher smiled smugly.

00:03:28.489 --> 00:03:31.040
“Let’s use the word… ‘expedition’.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.950
Has a nicer ring to it, don’t you think?”

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.099
“An expedition to where?” he asked.

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:38.450
“I’m afraid I can’t tell you that.”

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.790
“Then I won’t go,” Javi shrugged.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.460
“Listen closely, D-14164.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:49.590
The SCP Foundation has… we’ll say a considerable
influence across the globe.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:55.060
What we’re asking you to agree to is involvement
in possibly one of the most dangerous operations

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.129
we have ever conducted.

00:03:56.129 --> 00:04:00.220
Now, as unappealing as that might sound, allow
me to sweeten the deal.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:04.819
Should you say yes, agree to take part, and
follow our instructions, then you might find

00:04:04.819 --> 00:04:10.840
that the Foundation’s influence may be rather
beneficial to you… should you survive.”

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:15.820
The researcher paused to push a document across
the table, close enough for Javi to read.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:20.060
“A clean record, that one nasty mistake
wiped clean for good.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.979
On top of that, an immediate release and a
new identity.

00:04:22.979 --> 00:04:26.589
You’d have a second chance, Mr. Garrett.

00:04:26.589 --> 00:04:28.849
Both you and your daughter would.”

00:04:28.849 --> 00:04:30.629
“And what if I say no?”

00:04:30.629 --> 00:04:31.970
Javi asked bluntly.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:34.910
“Well, that’s your prerogative,” the
researcher replied.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:38.660
“And we won’t be able to detain you after
releasing evidence of your innocence.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.600
So, you’ll be free no matter what.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:45.330
Oh, although, your daughter will, of course,
be remanded into custody, given that she is

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.539
actually guilty.

00:04:46.539 --> 00:04:50.939
Maybe, once we get her move to D Class, she
might be more willing to cooperate than her

00:04:50.939 --> 00:04:52.740
dear old dad?”

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.830
Under the table, Javi’s hands were shaking
with rage.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:05:00.449
He clenched his fist so furiously that the
cuffs felt tighter around his wrists.

00:05:00.449 --> 00:05:04.219
The hate in his eyes was palpable as he glared
at the researcher.

00:05:04.219 --> 00:05:08.289
It was bad enough that they had backed him
into a corner, put him in a situation wherein

00:05:08.289 --> 00:05:11.039
saying yes or no would be equally catastrophic.

00:05:11.039 --> 00:05:16.339
But what felt worse was that they knew, they
knew what Kali had done, and they were using

00:05:16.339 --> 00:05:18.320
that as a threat.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:22.460
Taking a deep breath, Javi steadied himself
before finally speaking up again.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.759
“Just tell me what you want me to do.”

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:28.860
Instantly, he felt like he’d been thrown
headfirst into a commotion he could barely

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.119
keep up with.

00:05:30.119 --> 00:05:34.520
No sooner had he said that, Javi had been
led away by a team of Foundation guards while

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.530
the researcher followed, rattling off vague
information about the ‘expedition’.

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:44.100
Guided by the armed escort into another room,
Javi was flocked by more Foundation staff,

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:48.360
strapping electronic equipment over the outside
of his orange prisoner garb.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:53.180
One piece of it was to monitor his heart rate,
another was a portable camera to record his

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.199
surroundings,
although those were among the few details

00:05:56.199 --> 00:05:59.059
that he was actually able to catch during
all the activity.

00:05:59.059 --> 00:06:03.249
Javi couldn’t help noticing how nobody had
even mentioned just where he was meant to

00:06:03.249 --> 00:06:06.830
be going on this expedition,
just that the Foundation wanted to keep a

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:09.309
close eye on him while he was there.

00:06:09.309 --> 00:06:12.979
“You still haven’t told me exactly where
it is I’m meant to be going,” he finally

00:06:12.979 --> 00:06:13.979
spoke up.

00:06:13.979 --> 00:06:14.979
“Or how I’m getting there.”

00:06:14.979 --> 00:06:17.810
“All in good time,” the head researcher
replied.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:22.069
“So far, the only detail you need to be
aware of is this: it’s dangerous.

00:06:22.069 --> 00:06:24.659
A particularly hostile environment.”

00:06:24.659 --> 00:06:27.539
“So, like a warzone?”

00:06:27.539 --> 00:06:28.539
Javi asked.

00:06:28.539 --> 00:06:31.969
The researcher smiled, but to themselves,
as if there was something funny about the

00:06:31.969 --> 00:06:35.099
question and the lack of understanding it
conveyed.

00:06:35.099 --> 00:06:39.490
Javi’s attention was quickly turned to another
D Class, wearing a similar D Class uniform

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:40.490
to him.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:44.539
The staff began prepping the second convict
in the same room, although without nearly

00:06:44.539 --> 00:06:46.099
as much gear as they’d given Javi.

00:06:46.099 --> 00:06:49.009
“I thought I was the only one going on this
trip,” he stated.

00:06:49.009 --> 00:06:53.300
“Oh, don’t worry, that’s just the lure,”
the researcher explained, though it only raised

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.300
more questions.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.249
“They won’t be accompanying you.”

00:06:56.249 --> 00:07:00.690
It was then Javi was led out of the prep room,
and walked through the Foundation facility.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.469
The place was a hive of activity, as well
as noise.

00:07:03.469 --> 00:07:08.460
There were alien shrieks and wails, monstrous
sounds emanating from deep in the building,

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:13.759
muffled only slightly underneath thick layers
of concrete and heavy steel doors.

00:07:13.759 --> 00:07:20.289
On top of that, there were screams, too, distinctly
human sounds of pain and fear.

00:07:20.289 --> 00:07:24.830
Javi tried to ignore it as he was instructed
to keep walking, feeling almost nostalgic

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:27.740
for the clank of metal bars back at his old
cell.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:32.439
He had been anticipating being taken out of
the facility, towards maybe a helipad or runway

00:07:32.439 --> 00:07:36.689
where an aircraft would be waiting to fly
him out to his undisclosed destination.

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:41.349
In fact, even a dock with a moored boat would
have been more within the realm of what he

00:07:41.349 --> 00:07:42.349
was expected.

00:07:42.349 --> 00:07:47.099
But instead, he was taken deeper and deeper
into the Foundation’s sprawling complex,

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:51.629
passing testing areas and containment levels,
through winding corridors until...

00:07:51.629 --> 00:07:56.669
Javi was told to stop in front of a heavy
door that held a containment area beyond.

00:07:56.669 --> 00:08:01.539
He couldn’t help noticing that the door
itself looked brand new like it had only just

00:08:01.539 --> 00:08:02.539
been installed.

00:08:02.539 --> 00:08:07.189
Meanwhile, the frame surrounding it had traces
of discoloring and damage, almost as if something

00:08:07.189 --> 00:08:11.740
corrosive had melted away the previous door,
hence the replacement.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:13.219
“This is it?”

00:08:13.219 --> 00:08:18.089
Javi asked, confused but still trying to nudge
more information out of the Foundation staff.

00:08:18.089 --> 00:08:22.139
“You want me to do an ‘expedition’ within
your own building?”

00:08:22.139 --> 00:08:28.370
“Yes and no,” the head researcher replied,
still giving next to no useful details.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:29.959
“Now, this is important.

00:08:29.959 --> 00:08:33.430
Once you get to your destination, we need
you to figure out how to get back to us.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:37.960
You do that, and you’ll have your freedom,
your daughter, your second chance.”

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:41.200
“Surely to get back I can just open up this
door again?”

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.330
the prisoner said.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:47.220
That garnered a slight chuckle from the researcher,
again seeming to find Javi’s lack of understanding

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.640
amusing.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:51.460
“Oh, D-14164.

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:53.690
If only it was that simple.”

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:58.880
The door opened with a heaving, metallic creak,
and Javi was unceremoniously pushed inside

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:00.120
by the guards.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.940
Staggering inside, catching himself before
he lost his balance and fell over,

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:09.220
he almost turned back to start slamming his
fists against the now-sealed entrance.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:13.930
He would have, were it not for the sight of
something oozing out of the wall directly

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:15.030
in front of him.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:19.910
Javi stepped closer to inspect in, but withdrew
his hand as he noticed thick, black droplets

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:21.640
leaking onto the floor.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:26.910
The substance hissed as it made contact with
the ground, like it was burning through, corroding

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:29.250
whatever it came into contact with.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:32.950
Keeping himself from touching it, Javi leaned
in to get a closer look…

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:38.060
and found the grotesque face of SCP-106 looking
back at him.

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:42.750
A spindly, decrepit hand reached out of the
gooey puddle and grabbed the orange material

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.590
of Javi’s jumpsuit,
pulling at the garment with enough strength

00:09:45.590 --> 00:09:47.570
to tug his entire body forward.

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:52.440
In a blind panic, Javi tried to swipe the
Old Man’s rotting arm away, feeling an intense

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.870
burning,
almost like a chemical scalding his skin as

00:09:55.870 --> 00:10:01.870
the same black ooze burned through his clothing
and started to singe his chest.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:06.330
Another hand shot forward out of the puddle
on the wall, a clawed thumb puncturing Javi’s

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.330
side.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:10.630
He screamed in pain as he felt the blistering
digit pierce into him,

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:16.470
while the rest of the fingers pulled him closer
still to the wall, using the hole in his side

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:17.750
like a handle.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:22.950
The stench of his own burning flesh mixed
with the air of rotting decay that SCP-106

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.740
brought with it everywhere.

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:29.310
The decaying face of the Old Man peered through
the black slime on the wall,

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:35.760
its mouth locked in a sadistic, sinister grin
as Javi found himself pulled inside.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.550
It almost felt like he had fallen asleep in
the bathtub,

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:43.150
and woken up gasping and spluttering, just
having narrowly avoided drowning.

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:48.220
Except now he was waking up in an entirely
different space, the transition there having

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.230
done little to dull the pain of his injuries.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:55.580
Sitting up as he arrived in his new dark and
desolate surroundings, Javi gripped his side

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.860
and winced at the searing pain.

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:02.500
Then, the sudden smell of burning plastic
crawled up his nostrils and down the back

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.790
of his throat.

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:06.920
Most of the equipment the Foundation had strapped
onto him was melting;

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:12.220
the heart rate monitor and camera corroding,
covered in more of that black sludge.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:15.590
Standing up, gritting his teeth through the
pain of his wounds, Javi quickly removed the

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:17.840
devices as carefully as he could.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:22.170
He was far beyond caring about the Foundation’s
‘expedition’, right now, he just wanted

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:26.610
to get back out of… wherever the hell this
place was.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:30.690
Checking over his shoulder, the slick, corrosive
puddle he’d been pulled through was already

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:31.690
gone.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:36.279
At any rate, Javi didn’t particularly like
the idea of going back that way, so was relieved

00:11:36.279 --> 00:11:39.570
– although he’d soon find out that relief
was perhaps misplaced.

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:44.560
He had barely a few moments to examine his
surroundings, not that there was much he could

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:49.860
see besides endless dark corridors…
and the withered figure of the Old Man.

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:55.230
It had reappeared, looking like it was far
off in the distance before, in a split second,

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:59.110
the gap between SCP-106 and Javi had closed.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:04.300
The creature tilted its bald, skeletal head
as it looked at him, and he got a full, unobscured

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:09.510
glimpse at its sunken eyes and face locked
in a perpetual lipless grin.

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:14.310
The rotting, wrinkly flesh of the Old Man’s
body was oozing more and more of that dark,

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:17.790
disgusting mucus,
droplets of it landing on Javi’s clothing

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:19.930
and burning holes right through.

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:24.100
One hand still applying pressure to his side,
Javi turned and tried to run as far and fast

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.670
as his body was able.

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:30.380
If getting away was his sole objective, he
wanted out as quick as possible,

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:34.430
anything to get away from the nightmarish
creature he had now found himself trapped

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:35.430
with.

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:37.220
Running didn’t seem to work though.

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:39.430
He was sure he had made it at least a few
feet,

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:44.120
the Old Man was still standing behind him
but looked to be at more of a distance.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:49.300
That was, until Javi noticed his legs; they
were running backwards.

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:55.620
Each step he had taken away from SCP-106 was
being reversed, rewound like on an old VHS

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.710
tape,
bringing him back closer and closer to the

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.320
creature’s clutches.

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:04.190
Its claws pushed painfully through Javi’s
back as it reversed time right back to the

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:06.620
point where he had turned to run away.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:10.990
As the Old Man reached through him, more of
that burning, acidic pain starting eating

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:15.930
away at its captive D Class prey,
with Javi letting out a pained scream.

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:20.700
It wasn’t until several minutes in that
he realized something that hurt almost just

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:25.800
as bad:
SCP-106 could have killed him in an instant.

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.210
That much was clear.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:28.420
But it hadn’t.

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:30.520
It had chosen not to.

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:36.040
Instead, it was torturing him, prolonging
the pain Javi was experiencing…

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.660
because it wanted him to suffer.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:44.210
With all its strength, SCP-106 hurled him
several feet, until Javi’s burning, corroding

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:49.120
body collided with a hard surface, a wall,
with a loud crack.

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:52.840
The Old Man then manipulated the time within
his pocket dimension, causing Javi to fly

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:56.530
backward through the air,
back into the creature’s corrosive grip.

00:13:56.530 --> 00:14:01.840
It allowed time to keep winding back, undoing
all the damage it had done so far.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:06.180
As much as Javi was relieved to be rid of
the searing pain he was in, a sick worry deep

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:10.500
in the pit of his stomach told him that this
wasn’t an act of mercy;

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:14.830
the Old Man just wanted to make him suffer
all over again.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:21.510
He lost track of how long it went on for,
SCP-106 taking sick glee in hurting his captive,

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:25.890
only to reverse the time within the pocket
dimension and do it all again.

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:30.800
Each time felt just like the first, made worse
by the fact that Javi never had a chance to

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:34.120
get used to the pain, to become numb to it.

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:39.400
Instead, every moment the torture started
was just like the first time, in fact, it

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.020
technically was.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:45.640
Screaming in agony, Javi had no clue if he
had been there for hours, days, months, or

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:46.750
even years.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:49.040
Had any time passed at all?

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:51.670
How many times had the Old Man done this to
him,

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:57.120
only to reverse time and do it all over again,
letting the pain begin anew?

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:00.130
Every few tries, the Old Man would release
Javi for a moment.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:04.230
But once again, it was never done out of any
sense of mercy or kindness.

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:06.680
It was so it could hunt him.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:12.370
Still, Javi ran every time, as far and fast
as he could, searching every corner of the

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:15.170
dark, desolate place for some kind of way
out.

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:20.000
A portal home, another of those corrosive
black puddles, a big door with ‘Exit’

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.810
written on it in big red letters.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:30.380
But instead, all he found was SCP-106… or
rather, the Old Man found him.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:31.680
It was hunting him again.

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:34.380
Javi had no idea how many times this made.

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:38.030
Panting, he slowed to a halt, trying to catch
his breath.

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:42.870
Reaching out in the dark, he put a hand against
a nearby hard surface, a wall… then felt

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:44.850
a crack under his hand.

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:49.620
Examining closer, although he could barely
see it, Javi could feel, with absolute certainty,

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:52.370
that the wall had been damaged, just a little.

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:57.840
It was the same one, the exact same wall he
had been thrown against, who knew how long

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:58.840
ago.

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:03.860
But the point was, it was still cracked from
where his body had hit it, even after the

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:09.390
Old Man had reversed time to hurt Javi over
and over again, the damage had stayed.

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:14.250
He had no way of knowing if it would work,
or how long it would take, but it might have

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:16.340
been a way out.

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:19.980
Desperately, Javi slammed his fist against
the wall, feeling pain shooting through his

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:24.589
fingers and up into his arm as it collided
with the solid surface.

00:16:24.589 --> 00:16:26.070
Nothing changed.

00:16:26.070 --> 00:16:28.360
Winding back the other arm, he hit it again.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:29.360
Still nothing.

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:33.310
Javi could hear the Old Man shuffling closer
behind him, could sense his hands reaching

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:35.540
out closer to torture him again.

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:40.380
He let it happen, striking one last blow against
the wall before it finally reached him, and

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:46.590
the pain began once more,
only to be reversed so SCP-106 could do it

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:47.590
all again.

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:49.270
But now, he had a goal.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:53.800
Each time the creature rewound time and undid
all the damage to its captive’s body,

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:59.710
Javi went looking for that same wall, feeling
across every surface until he reached it again.

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:04.699
The damage was still there, only a tiny crack
for now, but time – despite being under

00:17:04.699 --> 00:17:09.189
the Old Man’s control in this pocket dimension
– was on Javi’s side.

00:17:09.189 --> 00:17:13.829
Whenever he made it back to the wall, he started
to punch at it again, pounding one fist against

00:17:13.829 --> 00:17:15.069
it after the other.

00:17:15.069 --> 00:17:19.689
He didn’t relent, despite the pain it caused
him, he told himself it would be worth it

00:17:19.689 --> 00:17:21.459
if it meant he made it out.

00:17:21.459 --> 00:17:25.350
Even the times when the bones in his hands
broke, and he was flimsily striking at the

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:28.970
cracked wall with shattered fingers, he didn’t
stop.

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:30.390
It would be worth it.

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:33.249
It had to be, no matter how long it took.

00:17:33.249 --> 00:17:37.129
He would gradually chip away at the wall,
more and more.

00:17:37.129 --> 00:17:42.169
Every time SCP-106 would find Javi, and when
it did, it would hurt him.

00:17:42.169 --> 00:17:46.200
The pain he’d put himself through trying
to break down the wall helped numb some of

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:49.789
the torture before the Old Man and reset everything
again.

00:17:49.789 --> 00:17:55.539
Then, the hunt began again, and Javi went
back to making his gradual dent in the wall.

00:17:55.539 --> 00:18:00.470
The whole time, he remembered he was doing
it for Kali, for his freedom, and a fresh

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:01.470
start.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:03.480
Until, eventually, it stopped.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:07.470
Javi had no idea how many times he’d struck
the wall, but it had been enough to start

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:10.840
tunneling through it slightly, both hands
bloody and broken again.

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:13.389
But this time, the Old Man didn’t appear.

00:18:13.389 --> 00:18:14.909
It had stopped.

00:18:14.909 --> 00:18:18.269
Screaming in rage, Javi started throwing himself
at the indented wall, trying desperately to

00:18:18.269 --> 00:18:22.970
chip away more,
completely unaware that SCP-106 had left him

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:25.640
alone in its pocket dimension.

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:29.580
Back in their facility, the Foundation had
lost contact with Javi’s recording devices

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:33.370
over three hours ago,
at which point they had initiated their Recall

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:36.350
Protocol,
injuring the D Class they had chosen as a

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:37.350
lure.

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:41.080
Sure enough, the Old Man had reappeared from
his pocket dimension, following the pained

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:43.679
screams to come and finish the lure off.

00:18:43.679 --> 00:18:48.720
There was no sign of Javi, and with a sigh,
the head researcher simply noted down:

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:51.491
‘SCP-106 Pocket Dimension Escape Test.

00:18:51.491 --> 00:18:54.330
Result: test inconclusive.’

00:18:54.330 --> 00:19:01.010
Now go check out SCP-106 CONTAINMENT BREACH”
and “SCP-106 CAUSED A SCHOOL LOCKDOWN”

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:05.269
for stories of a few other situations where
unsuspecting victims found themselves being

00:19:05.269 --> 00:19:10.049
hunted by the Old Man... and whether or not
they too lived to talk about it.

